verdicts.checked:
Walked the sequence: foreign_keys OFF outside a transaction, BEGIN, SQL, foreign_key_check, user_version, COMMIT, ON. Then checked:
- the 12-step rebuild (create new_users, copy, DROP users, rename) with foreign keys off;
- DROP with foreign keys on and ON DELETE CASCADE, which deletes the children and returns no error, so the prescribed test fails on the buggy runner;
- user_version set inside the transaction: it lives in the header page and rolls back with the transaction;
- foreign_key_check runs whatever the foreign_keys setting;
- a migration file that itself contains BEGIN fails loudly ('cannot start a transaction within a transaction');
- the injection seam: design-2's openWith(path, fs.FS).

verdicts.instead:
Build design-2's classes:
- cleaned: //admin/ and /admin/../admin/ get 301 to /admin/; //admin gets 301 to /admin;
- case: /ADMIN and /ADMIN/ get 404;
- gated: /admin, /admin/, /%61dmin, /%61dmin/, /admin/%2e%2e/admin/, /admin/does-not-exist and every adminRoutes path.

Use the invariant 'no 2xx, no marker, and Location is /admin, /admin/, exactly /auth/github/login, or begins /auth/github/login?'. Restate the precondition as holding because adminMux is referenced only inside the two RequireOwner mounts.

In the internal test in package auth, serve OwnerRoute three requests:
- a bare one;
- one whose context holds an Identify Viewer for a non-owner;
- one whose context holds a Viewer with IsOwner=true but no Owner proof.

Expect 403 and zero calls each time. Add a fourth with the Owner proof set the way RequireOwner sets it: expect one call, receiving that Owner.
